[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4990453746","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121401#issuecomment-4990453746","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121401","id":4990453746,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKXRH8g","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T09:47:56Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T09:47:56Z","body":"The crash traces to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/49f68a134ec7997dda2eb5b92a1f43eb37273498/editor/script/script_editor_plugin.cpp#L1868\r\nFor some reason the `_connect_to_scene_recursive()` is called with null nodes (idk if null or freed, but they show as `0x0` in the debugger). Removing `CONNECT_DEFERRED` fixes it somehow.\r\n\r\nCC @kitbdev ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4990453746/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4993002156","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121401#issuecomment-4993002156","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121401","id":4993002156,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKZsqrA","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-16T14:22:43Z","updated_at":"2026-07-16T14:22:43Z","body":"I guess its not safe to connect to `child_entered_tree` deferred? In case its argument gets deleted.\r\nMaking it not deferred means that the owner won't be set in time for the check.\r\nTo fix it, we could remove the `if (p_current != p_base && p_current->get_owner() != p_base)` check entirely in `ScriptEditor::_connect_to_scene_recursive`. It would cause it to connect to editable children, but it shouldn't affect behavior since `_find_scripts` would still have the check.\r\nOr we could make the method use ObjectIDs instead to check for validity, and have the signal connect to another method that calls this one deferred with the ids.\r\n\r\n(Actually I just realized that scripts on Nodes that are children of editable children, but that are still owned by the parent scene aren't detected for highlighting, maybe `_find_scripts` should check through its children even if they aren't owned.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4993002156/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5415308925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121401#issuecomment-5415308925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121401","id":5415308925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQscOfQ","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-25T19:04:07Z","updated_at":"2026-08-25T19:04:07Z","body":"Strangely enough, I can't reproduce the crash I mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121401#pullrequestreview-4708299812 on Linux, under the same conditions with this PR rebased on top of `master` https://github.com/godotengine/godot/commit/b56a91878e